{"title": "Hag", "pageid": 19885, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Hag", "categories": ["Creatures", "Hags", "Races", "Non-playable races"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/37/Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png/300px-Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/37/Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png/450px-Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/37/Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png/600px-Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/37/Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png/300px-Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"601\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/3/37/Auntie_Ethel_Hag_Model.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption><div class=\"noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable\">  A hag in Baldur's Gate 3  </div></figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Hags</b> are a non-playable <a href=\"/wiki/Fey\" title=\"Fey\">Fey</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Race\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Race\">Race</a> in <i><a href=\"/wiki/Baldur%27s_Gate_3\" title=\"Baldur's Gate 3\">Baldur's Gate 3</a></i>. They are clever, highly magical creatures who delight in the suffering they cause. Their power is further increased by their collections of magical trinkets, created by the Hag over the years.\n</p>\n<div class=\"noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable\">\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r356266\">.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{display:grid;margin:10px 4px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{padding:8px 16px;margin:auto}@media screen and (max-width:779px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-top:10px;padding:8px 2px;border-left:0!important;grid-row:2;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:3;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote{justify-content:center!important}}@media screen and (min-width:780px){.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left{margin-left:10px;border-left:2px solid #3d3d3d!important;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-right{margin-right:10px;border-left:0!important;border-right:2px solid #3d3d3d;grid-row:1;grid-column:2}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-right{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:3}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left{margin:auto 0;grid-row:1;grid-column:1}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{grid-row:2;grid-column:2}}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author{margin-left:auto;margin-right:32px;font-size:smaller;font-weight:bold}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{font-size:300%;font-family:serif;color:#3d3d3d;line-height:1em}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin{margin-bottom:auto;margin-right:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end{margin-top:auto;margin-left:8px}.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text{font-style:italic}</style><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote\" style=\"justify-content: left\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-image-left\" style=\"display: inline-block; width: 100px; height: 100px; clip-path: xywh(0 0 100% 100% round 15%);\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/100px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/150px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/100px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span><blockquote style=\"font-size: 110%\" class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-blockquote-left\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center\">\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-begin\">“</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-text\">Soothsayers, invaders of dreams, dark ritualists, saviours, murderers: hags are all of these and more.</div>\n     <div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-end\">„</div>\n  </div>\n</blockquote><div class=\"bg3wiki-fancy-quote-author\">— In-game racial description</div><div style=\"grid-column:3\"></div></div>\n</div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"About_Hags\">About Hags</span></h2>\n<p>According to <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Evil_Eye\" title=\"The Evil Eye\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/10/Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png/30px-Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/10/Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png/40px-Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/10/Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png/20px-Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/10/Book_Tome_Q_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Evil_Eye\" title=\"The Evil Eye\">The Evil Eye</a> there are three known kinds of hags: Green Hags, Sea Hags, and Night Hags. Night Hags are named after their ability to haunt a mortal's dreams. They slowly devour the mortal's vital essense, collecting it in their soul bag. They are known to be petty and selfish, and prone to bragging. Sea Hags are said to smell of fish, and prefer to eat their victims whole. They can kill with a glance. Green Hags can appear as beautiful mortals, are very dangerous, and are quick to anger.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hag_characters\">Hag characters</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/30px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/45px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/60px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Auntie Ethel\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/30px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\">Auntie Ethel</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Related_items\">Related items</span></h2>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r347748\">.mw-parser-output .div-col{margin-top:0.3em;column-width:20em}.mw-parser-output .div-col>ul{list-style-type:inherit}.mw-parser-output .div-col-rules{column-rule:1px solid #aaa}.mw-parser-output .div-col dl,.mw-parser-output .div-col ol,.mw-parser-output .div-col ul{margin-top:0}.mw-parser-output .div-col li,.mw-parser-output .div-col dd{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}</style><div class=\"div-col\">\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-uncommon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki